    "sources": [
      {
        "id": "source_24ac5ec7w28f4fj00jdgambb69",
        "artist_id": "artist_3qmp7zjbg1rpebhtyfy43096vj",
        "show_id": "show_3n03w01p0513amd3cc3c1fqfwt",
        "display_date": "1973-10-30",
        "is_soundboard": false,
        "is_remaster": false,
        "has_jamcharts": false,
        "avg_rating": 0.0,
        "num_reviews": 0,
        "num_ratings": null,
        "avg_rating_weighted": 4.544534683227539,
        "duration": 11845.0,
        "upstream_identifier": "gd1973-10-30.170339.aud.lamarre.vernon.sirmick.flac2496",
        "description": "<div class=\"b1 set\"><span>Set I</span><div class=\"set_info\" style=\"padding-left:1em;\"><span title=\"Click to edit\">Here Comes Sunshine<br />Me and My Uncle<br />Ramble on Rose<br />Looks Like Rain<br />Deal<br />Mexicali Blues<br />They Love Each Other<br />El Paso<br />Row Jimmy<br />Jack Straw<br />China Cat Sunflower &gt;<br />I Know You Rider<br />Playing in the Band</span></div></div><div class=\"b2 set\"><span>Set II</span><div class=\"set_info\" style=\"padding-left:1em;\"><span title=\"Click to edit\">Mississippi Half-Step (Uptown Toodleloo)<br />Big River<br />Dark Star &gt;<br />Mind Left Body Jam &gt;<br />Dark Star &gt;<br />Stella Blue &gt;<br />Eyes of the World &gt;<br />Weather Report Suite &gt;<br />Goin' Down the Road Feeling Bad &gt;<br />Johnny B. Goode<br />encore:<br />One More Saturday Night</span></div></div><div class=\"b1 set\"><div class=\"set_info\" style=\"padding-left:1em;\"><span title=\"Click to edit\">\u00a0</span></div></div><div class=\"b2 set\"><span>Comment</span><div class=\"set_info\" style=\"padding-left:1em;\"><span title=\"Click to edit\">Released in Listen to the River: '71, '72, '73 Box Set<br /><br />Jerry Garcia - Guitar<br />Bob Weir - Guitar<br />Keith Godchaux - Keyboards<br />Phil Lesh - Bass<br />Bill Kreutzmann - Drums<br />Donna Jean Godchaux - Vocals</span></div></div>",
        "taper_notes": "Comments:\n\n- It's known that there is another audience recording of this show taped by Karl Ryan which\n  contains both \"Jack Straw\" and \"Dark Star\", I'm hopeful that I may be able to obtain a copy.\n\n\nNotes:\n\n- All tracks pitch corrected\n- The tape was paused between most tracks, these have been smoothed out.\n- This derives from the same master as Shnid 154414 which has been used to patch the last 1:51 of\n  \"El Paso\", there are also several smaller patches for continuity purposes. Thank you Andrew F.\n- Shnid 32367 has been used to patch in the whole of \"Jack Straw\" and \"Dark Star\" except for the\n  last 2:52 - Thanks to Charlie Miller. Both of these tracks have been remixed to mono, as has the\n  last part of \"El Paso\", so  that they are a better fit.\n- The first 38 seconds or so of \"Let It Grow\" have some tape damage, so it has been matrixed with\n   the soundboard to repair it.\n- There is some tape damage in \"Johnny B. Goode\", this has also been matrixed.\n- There is a 56 second patch in GDTRFB and several others, for continuity, in set II.\n- The vocals were quite low in places and have been boosted.\n- Some background noise has been removed.\n\n\nThanks to Doug Lamarre for providing his tapes.\n\nThanks to Matt Vernon for the transfer and for facilitating.\n\n\nedited and mastered\nSIRMick\nFebruary 2025",
        "source": "Audience recording (low gen) from the collection of  Doug Lamarre",
        "taper": "",
        "transferrer": "",
        "lineage": "Transfer: Cassette > Nakamichi CR-7A #1 (azimuth adjusted, Dolby B) > Tascam DA-3000 #2 (DSF 1-bit/5.6 MHz) > Tascam Hi Res Editor (DSF concatenate & 2496 PCM) - transfer  by Matt Vernon Lineage: wav 24/96 > iZotope RX 11 Advanced > iZotope Neutron 5 >CD Wave > Flac24",
        "flac_type": "Flac24Bit",
